{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466931-pharaoh\u2019s-lightkeepers-alliance-especulation","id":1466931,"title":"Pharaoh\u2019s Lightkeepers: Alliance especulation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-06T05:55:40-07:00","id":1466931,"title":"Pharaoh\u2019s Lightkeepers: Alliance especulation","content":"In the Trinity Continuum, no alliance is more mysterious than the Pharaoh\u2019s Lightkeepers. This is by design to let us shape them into whatever we need. That said, I think it would be fun to share our theories regarding their origin and secret goals.<br /> <br /> Now, I will start with the most obvious one. Their leader Pharos is none other than Max Mercer. My personal theory is that <b>SPOILER</b> Mercer created the lightkeepers at the dawn of human civilization in Ancient Egypt to fight his evil future self through history. The organization has fallen and risen multiple times over the ages, but their leader Pharos has always been Max, and perhaps someone else on occasion when Max couldn't be there. Only a select few lightkeepers know about the truth that the organization isn't just fighting regular evil, but an evil pharaoh of the future hell-bent on creating his &quot;perfect&quot; timeline, even if it means enslaving humanity.<br /> <br /> So, what do you think? Do you have any other cool theories?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 01-18-2022, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T07:09:25-07:00","id":1466937,"title":"","content":"Like a Dark Pharaoh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T07:13:32-07:00","id":1466938,"title":"","content":"My theories are 3:<br /> <br /> 1. Pharos created the Light Keepers sometime before Hammersmith event. He is a Stalwart, super intelligent and long lived, probably inspired during the Aether era when the first signs of the Light Keepers appears.<br /> <br /> 2. Pharos is like Apocalypse from X-men, but not evil. He was born in Ancient Egypt and has been living since, helping people and saving the world. Probably a psiad with VK and Clair, living in a secret place where he kept some of the scrolls of Alexandria library that he expanded over the years.<br /> <br /> 3. He is from the future and somehow send messages to the past to shape the world to what it is in his time (I recently watched TENET, and it\u2019s a new theory)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T08:22:11-07:00","id":1466948,"title":"","content":"Given that every single survivor of the Hammersmith event became Inspired, you do have to wonder if Dr. Hammersmith had some way of determining beforehand whether someone had Inspired potential and was setting up a mass Inspiration event. Given that his Telluric Engine was probably a super science device, that pretty much required him to be Inspired himself.<br /> <br /> Maybe Hammersmith was Pharos and used the secret knowledge of ancient cultures to identify Inspired potential. Now that he is dead, another Lightkeeper had taken his place. Was the Hammersmith explosion really an accident, or was it sabotage be enemies of the Lightkeepers or a rival within the organization?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T13:02:56-07:00","id":1466978,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Pharos is Emma Nazir. It would be a nice callback to the original Adventure! I'd like some more callbacks like that. I was a bit disappointed that Sara Kaur took the place of Jackson Harley as, I assume, the super powered Psiad that was created from the Hammersmith Event. The Sara Kaur lore and how she plays into later events is interesting, don't get me wrong but I don't think she necessarily needed to be tied into that event and Jackson Harley getting empowered and using his great power for essentially parlor tricks was interesting to me. Not everybody who got power from the Hammersmith Event needed to become a secret manipulator behind the scenes of history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T16:39:53-07:00","id":1466994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466931-pharaoh\u2019s-lightkeepers-alliance-especulation?p=1466978#post1466978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not everybody who got power from the Hammersmith Event needed to become a secret manipulator behind the scenes of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>S.K. Bhurano technically wasn't a secret behind the scenes manipulator. She did some work with/for Mercer, corresponded with Dr. Primoris (who mostly insulted her), advocated for Indian independence, and supported equality for women, but wasn't really a secret manipulator. She mostly spent 200 years earning an absurd number of doctorate degrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T17:34:20-07:00","id":1467002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466931-pharaoh\u2019s-lightkeepers-alliance-especulation?p=1466938#post1466938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theories are 3:<br /> <br /> 1. Pharos created the Light Keepers sometime before Hammersmith event. He is a Stalwart, super intelligent and long lived, probably inspired during the Aether era when the first signs of the Light Keepers appears.<br /> <br /> 2. Pharos is like Apocalypse from X-men, but not evil. He was born in Ancient Egypt and has been living since, helping people and saving the world. Probably a psiad with VK and Clair, living in a secret place where he kept some of the scrolls of Alexandria library that he expanded over the years.<br /> <br /> 3. He is from the future and somehow send messages to the past to shape the world to what it is in his time (I recently watched TENET, and it\u2019s a new theory)</div> </div> </div> </div>I put Pharos as starting the Lightkeepers in the late 18th century, but they were definitely active during the Aether period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T21:29:02-07:00","id":1467013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466931-pharaoh\u2019s-lightkeepers-alliance-especulation?p=1466994#post1466994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S.K. Bhurano technically wasn't a secret behind the scenes manipulator. She did some work with/for Mercer, corresponded with Dr. Primoris (who mostly insulted her), advocated for Indian independence, and supported equality for women, but wasn't really a secret manipulator. She mostly spent 200 years earning an absurd number of doctorate degrees.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh I just have the Core book and the Aeon book. In the Aeon book she was responsible for the events that unintentionally brought the attention of the Doyen to humanity unlike had ever happened before. It's true she wasn't really a manipulator and she seemed to actively tried to keep below the radar of others but she was working towards a goal of understanding the Hammersmith Event and Humanity's potential. She wasn't forming secret societies but she did have big plans that eventually had world changing consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-14T07:51:05-08:00","id":1467789,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Pharos is a Doyen. Possessing new hosts since Ancient Egypt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T11:17:39-08:00","id":1468157,"title":"","content":"The couple things I have noted:<ul><li>Pharos is mentioned as leading a group with almost the same description in the Adventure! backer preview.</li> <li>The Lightkeepers emblem is a lighthouse in a pyramid</li> <li>In TC: Aeon, there doesn't appear (in the books I have) to be any mention of Pharos, Lodestar or Lightkeepers, but the very mysterious and only controlled via the Aeon Council Section Minerva uses lighthouse-shaped pins to identify themselves.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T15:11:54-08:00","id":1468184,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Lightkeepers were absorbed into the Aeon Trinity and became Section Minerva at some point in the 21st or early 22nd century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T15:38:40-08:00","id":1468185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1466931-pharaoh\u2019s-lightkeepers-alliance-especulation?p=1468184#post1468184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the Lightkeepers were absorbed into the Aeon Trinity and became Section Minerva at some point in the 21st or early 22nd century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that's why I have such a strong suspicion that Max is Pharos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}